{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall make the ephod.</b> It implies one, yet it is written 'and the ephod went with him,' and eighty priests bearing an ephod of linen. Answer: an ephod without gold, and Israel would inquire only by the choshen, in which were the urim and tumim. And what is written 'bring near the ephod' — there the choshen was joined to it. <b>And they shall make the ephod.</b> Here is the order of the making of the ephod and the choshen according to the verses. According to Rashi's method there is proof that the ephod is a garment, as we translate: 'and David was girded with an ephod of linen' — כדרוט דבוץ, and we find: 'so shall the king's daughters wear mantles' — we translate כדרוטין."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:50.807677525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}